            <ArticleTitle>[Emergency laparoscopy in the examination of middle-aged and elderly patients with acute surgical diseases of the abdominal cavity].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>124-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Urgent laparoscopies were performed on 566 elderly and senile patients suspected of acute surgical diseases of abdominal organs. Laparoscopic examinations proved to be highly informative in 90.4%, little informative in 6.6%, erroneous in 3% of cases. Wide use of urgent laparoscopies in elderly and senile patients allowed to avoid laparotomies in 62.3% of the cases. High curative-diagnostic efficiency of laparoscopies added by laparoscopic cholecystostomy and antegrade cholecystocholangiography in patients with acute cholecystitis, cholecystopancreatitis, mechanical jaundice has been shown.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
